{"seconds": 72.2, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! So the line is:\n- **Rc1+** \n- If Kd2, then Rd1+ Ke3 Rc3+ Ke2 Rd2+ Kf1 Rc1# (mate in 6 moves for Black)\n- If Ke2, then R8c2+ Ke3 Re1# (mate in 3 moves for Black)\n\nSo White's best try is Kd2, which delays mate the longest. The key move is **Rc1+**!\n\nThis is a **fork** pattern - the initial check forces the king to move, and then Black's rooks coordinate to deliver mate on the back rank. The motif is using a **backRankMate** pattern along with **fork/deflection** to drive the king into the corner.\n\n**Coaching note:**\nWhen the opponent's king is exposed and you have both rooks active, look for forcing checks that coordinate your rooks. Rc1+ here forces White's king into a deadly corridor\u2014both king moves lose, but Kd2 allows a back-rank mating pattern where your rooks alternate checks, driving the king forward until it has no escape squares. The lesson: rooks on the second and back rank can be devastating when the king lacks escape squares.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rc1+\", \"line\": [\"Rc1+\", \"Kd2\", \"Rd1+\", \"Ke3\", \"Rc3+\", \"Ke2\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"backRankMate\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2r5/5R2/4B1k1/1p2pR2/p3p3/8/PPr2PPP/3K4 b - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2r5/5R2/4B1k1/1p2pR2/p3p3/8/PPr2PPP/3K4 b - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2r5/5R2/4B1k1/1p2pR2/p3p3/8/PPr2PPP/3K4 b - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r5/5R2/4B1k1/1p2pR2/p3p3/8/PPr2PPP/3K4 b - - 1 32", "move": "Rd2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r5/5R2/4B1k1/1p2pR2/p3p3/8/PP1r1PPP/3K4 w - - 2 33", "move": "Ke1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r5/5R2/4B1k1/1p2pR2/p3p3/8/PPr2PPP/3K4 b - - 1 32", "move": "Rc1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r5/5R2/4B1k1/1p2pR2/p3p3/8/PP3P